course: dictionary
lesson: 8872
title: Comparing with shorter
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shorter is the comparing form of short. Use it when you want to say that one thing has less length, or is less tall, than another thing. «Tom is shorter than Max» means Tom has less height than Max.
explain: Shorter can also talk about time. «a shorter way home» is a way that takes less time or distance to get home. Shorter always compares, so ask yourself: shorter than what? Look for the word than, or for a thing the sentence has already named.
explain: Look closely at «The five-letter word "short" becomes "shorter" when you add two letters.» Short has five letters and shorter has seven, so the new word is longer on the page, yet it means less length. Spelling and meaning are not always the same thing.
fact: Shorter is the comparing form of short: short, shorter, shortest.
fact: Shorter means having less length than something else.
fact: Shorter can mean less tall, as in «Tom is shorter than Max».
fact: Shorter can mean lasting less time, as in «a shorter way home».
fact: «Shorter» has seven letters, and «short» has five: two letters were added to make it.
exercise: «Tom is shorter than Max.» Who is taller? | Nobody knows | *Max | Tom | They are the same height
exercise: «Take the shorter path home.» What does shorter mean here? | Full of ice | More steps, going up a hill | *Less time or distance | Less tall
exercise: «The five-letter word "short" becomes "shorter" when you add two letters.» Find and copy the word that is the comparing form of short. | letters | becomes | five | *shorter
test: «Ben's pencil is shorter than mine.» Which pencil is longer? | Neither has a length | Mine | Both are the same length | *Ben's pencil is longer than mine? No, mine
test: Pick the right word: «Jack is ___ than his big brother.» | shortest | taller | shorten | *shorter
exam: What does «a shorter way home» mean? | A way that goes up a steep hill | A sad way home | A way home that is longer than before | *A way that takes less time or distance
